/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Example_FiltersBiquad Biquad
 * @ingroup DspCore_Examples_Filters
 * @brief Visualize a 12 kHz low-pass/high-pass Biquad handoff.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_FiltersBiquad_Goal Goal
 * Send a 1--200 kHz logarithmic sine sweep through complementary low-pass and
 * high-pass Biquads at 480 kHz, with a 12 kHz cutoff and Q=0.7071.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_FiltersBiquad_Run Run and render
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_Filters_Biquad_d --output ./output
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/render_signal.sh ./output/biquad_sweep.csv
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_FiltersBiquad_Output Output
 * @code{.text}
 * DspCore :: Biquad 12 kHz low-pass / high-pass sweep
 * Wrote signal data: ./output/biquad_sweep.csv
 * PNG: .../render_signal.sh ./output/biquad_sweep.csv
 * @endcode
 *
 * The upper plot is a short RMS envelope of the temporal sweep, so the handoff
 * remains readable. The lower plot is the direct, coefficient-derived response
 * on a logarithmic frequency axis. Its guides identify the 12 kHz crossover and
 * -3 dB point.
 *
 * \image html biquad_sweep.png "Biquad crossover tutorial output" width=900px
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_FiltersBiquad_Code Desktop data generator
 * \include Filters/Biquad/Desktop/main.cpp
 *
 * @subsection DspCore_Example_FiltersBiquad_Kernel Portable Biquad API use
 * \include Filters/Biquad/Shared.cpp
 */
